  "limitations": [
    "Collision values are mean-radius capsule proxies, not skin-mesh intersections. Same-hand proximal/proximal webbing is excluded.",
    "Score-hold coverage includes planned early release and finger reuse; explicit controller firm phases are scored separately when metadata exists.",
    "Onset contact requires the assigned pad on the exposed physical key top within 2 mm, with key depth at least 0.5; key-onset alone can overstate playing accuracy.",
    "All score notes remain in the onset denominator. Holds/releases at clip end or near restrikes are censored and reported in full QA artifacts.",
    "Only 53 note onsets and 704 held note-frames are sampled in the three matched main windows. No whole-piece accuracy claim follows.",
    "The short fresh crossing probes choose different hand roles from the long historical clip; they do not reproduce its severe arm crossover. The historical replay evidence is separate.",
    "The 248-second window is an ordinary overlapping-hands regression, not the historical video glitch at performed 287.9-291.9 seconds.",
    "Final v4 Debussy still has 34/48 interhand capsule-overlap frames above 3 mm, worse than baseline 4/48; exact skin mesh checks must decide severity.",
    "Wide-chord final onset/hold contact trades off against v3 (24 vs 26 onsets, 136 vs 151 held frames), while final separation and temporal reversal metrics improve.",
    "Joint-speed violation threshold is 12.02 rad/s to allow exported time/angle rounding. Reversal rate is a motion proxy, not a perceptual realism score.",
    "Older baseline/v1 run manifests captured only three solver hashes; their recorded subset still matches frozen source. Newer manifests also verify six files unchanged through the run.",
